      "content": "# Introduction to the Authentication Module\nThis guide provides a comprehensive overview of our new authentication system designed to secure user access.\n\n# Authentication Flow Overview\nUnderstand the high-level workflow users experience from login to session management.\n\n# Registration Process\nLearn the steps required for new users to create secure accounts with email verification.\n\n# Login and Password Reset\nDiscover how users can log in securely and recover Forgotten credentials via email tokens.\n\n# Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)\nExplore the optional security layer allowing users to add a secondary verification method.\n\n# API Integration\nDevelopers can implement custom auth logic using our OAuth2 compliant server-side endpoints.\n\n# Security Best Practices\nReview critical guidelines for hashing passwords and managing session tokens effectively.\n\n# Error Handling Codes\nRefer to the specific HTTP status codes and messages returned during failed authentication attempts.\n\n# Module Controls\nAdmins can configure global settings like forced password expiration and lockout policies.\n\n# Conclusion\nBy following this structured documentation, you ensure a robust and maintainable authentication solution.",
